  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ARTISANAL FISHING COMMUNITIES WORK MORE SAFELY TO PREVENT DROWNING IN TANZANIA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall aim of the project is for artisanal fishing communities to work more safely to prevent drowning in Tanzania, and globally through shared learning. The current project, which will build on work commenced under RNLI Ireland&#x2019;s previous CSF grant, will seek to scale-up a package of effective drowning prevention interventions to foster safer work in artisanal fishing communities in selected districts around Lake Victoria. It will also aim to support civil society advocacy whilst convening government, specialists and UN agencies to develop policies and amplify lessons globally. By 2028, (phase 3) sufficient learning will embed drowning prevention strategies to promote safer work and prevent drowning on a wider scale in Tanzania and beyond.</narrative>
  </description>
